  "note": "Election of 12 members for the two wards of Warrenpoint Urban District on 17 May 1961: East Ward 5 seats, West Ward 7. The five Unionist members for East Ward were returned unopposed; West Ward was contested. Fourteen candidates contested the ward; the defeated candidates' totals were not printed. Only two outgoing councillors, Fay and McGreevy, were re-elected."
